div.p:
—Respond to the interest of the Eastern Europeans—as already expressed to us in
                    recent days on a number of occasions—in finding ways to prevent U.S.-Soviet differences from adversely affecting
                    their relations with us and with the West as a whole;

—Preserve, to the degree possible, the progress (in trade, claims negotiations,
                    family reunification, etc.) we have achieved in our relations with the Eastern
                    European countries;

—Reassure the West Europeans by demonstrating that we remain sensitive to their
                    special stake in good East-West relations and their desire to continue an
                    activist policy in Eastern Europe;
